  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed roof terrace and glazed roof access hatch due to their scale, design and location, would be prominent, visually intrusive and discordant features that would result in harm to the character and appearance of the host property and streetscene. The development is therefore contrary to policies LP1 and LP5 of the Wandsworth Local Plan (2023) and the Wandsworth Housing SPD (2016). \r\n\r\n",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposed roof terrace, by reason of its scale, design and location, would be an unneighbourly form of development that would result in loss of privacy, noise and disturbance to occupiers of neighbouring properties to the harm of their residential amenities. The development is therefore contrary to policy LP2 Wandsworth Local Plan (2023) and the Wandsworth Housing SPD (2016). ",
    "Reason : 3 - In dealing with this application the Council has implemented the requirement in the National Planning Policy Framework to work with the applicant in a positive and proactive manner and the Council has, as far as practicable, sought solutions to problems arising in relation to dealing with the planning application. We have made available detailed advice in the form of our statutory policies in the Local Plan and Supplementary Planning documents and where appropriate the Site Specific Allocations Document as well as offering a full pre application advice service. However, we have been unable to seek solutions to problems as the principle of the proposal is clearly contrary to our statutory policies and negotiation could not overcome the reasons for refusal."
  ],
